{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EKsCbyVW5v2RAiocdrZXwH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! There's a metric `prover.openings.stacked_reduction.mle_rounds_time_ms` which is a SUB-metric of the stacked reduction under openings. And `prover.rap_constraints.mle_rounds_time_ms` is a DIFFERENT metric under constraints.\n\nSo both the \"MLE Rounds\" under Constraints and the \"Stacked Reduction\" under Openings have MLE rounds. But spec.py maps them differently:\n- `app_rap_mle_rounds_time_ms` = sum of `prover.rap_constraints.mle_rounds_time_ms` → shown as \"MLE Rounds\" under Constraints\n\n\n- `app_openings_stacked_reduction_time_ms` = sum of `prover.openings.stacked_reduction_time_ms` → shown as \"Stacked Reduction\" under Openings\n\nThe `prover.openings.stacked_reduction_time_ms` captures the entire stacked reduction duration including both round 0 and the MLE rounds, while `prover.openings.stacked_reduction.mle_rounds_time_ms` isolates just the MLE portion. Since my code change affects `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval`, which is the MLE round function within stacked reduction, the timing impact should show up in that MLE sub-metric.\n\nThe \"MLE Rounds\" metric displayed in spec.py output actually refers to `prover.rap_constraints.mle_rounds_time_ms`, which is a separate MLE computation for constraint evaluation rather than stacked reduction. So the optimization wouldn't have affected that metric at all. Looking at the actual results, the \"Stacked Reduction\" metric improved from 123ms to 75ms at APC 300, confirming the change did work on the right component—the confusion was just about which MLE rounds metric we were targeting.\n\nNow I need to dig into the metrics JSON to see if `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` is also called during the constraint MLE rounds computation, and to get a clearer picture of the performance breakdown.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1442,"cache_read_input_tokens":90079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1442},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03176189-f3e8-4185-8773-a32af1748382","uuid":"b9955757-e8a8-44ef-b2d8-144480fd67d4"}
